(c) Cauchy criterion mechanics -- absolute integrability => Cauchy
==============================================================================
Standard real-analysis fact (not something to 'verify' symbolically,
but let's sanity check the FTC identity h(Y2)-h(Y1)=int_{Y1}^{Y2}h'(y)dy
underlying it, plus that the tail bound gives a genuine Cauchy tail):
This is the fundamental theorem of calculus, standard and not in
dispute; the target invokes it correctly as 'standard'.
int_{Y1}^{Y2} C/(x+y)^2 dy = C*(-Y1 + Y2)/((Y1 + x)*(Y2 + x))
As Y1,Y2 -> infinity (with Y2>Y1), this tail -> 0: standard Cauchy tail.
PASS (mechanics confirmed, standard fact correctly invoked).

